# Base URL of the existing, already-deployed Fashion Feet public REST API
# (the Next.js app in the repository root, routes under /api/v1).
#
# Expo inlines every variable prefixed with EXPO_PUBLIC_ into the bundle at build
# time, so after changing this value you must restart `npx expo start`
# (add `--clear` if the old value seems to stick).
#
# For the current deployed API, use https://fashion-feet-storefront.vercel.app
# until the custom fashionfeet.co.in DNS is configured.
# For local development, pick the value that matches how your device reaches the development machine:
#   Android emulator  -> http://10.0.2.2:3000        <-- NOT localhost
#   iOS simulator     -> http://localhost:3000
#   Physical device   -> http://<your-LAN-IP>:3000   (same Wi-Fi as the phone)
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and adjust. `.env` is git-ignored.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://10.0.2.2:3000
